# Avinash agentic SOP (Cursor)

This repository follows the **Avinash Agentic Software Design Pattern Catalog**. Do not improvise a one-shot prompt workflow.

## Required reading (progressive)

1. `PROJECT.yaml` — project control plane (status, systems, policies, overlays).
2. `AGENTS.md` — **this project's** constraints (not reusable skill text).
3. Skill `.agents/skills/avi-agentic-engineering/SKILL.md` — operating loop for substantial work.
4. Retrieve catalog cards only as needed from `.agents/skills/avi-agentic-engineering/references/catalog.md` (`AVI-AGENT-001` … `060`).

Do **not** dump the full catalog into context on every turn (`AVI-AGENT-033`, `AVI-AGENT-034`).

## Canonical loop

`Intent → inspect → plan → scoped implement → policy-gated tools → verify with evidence → independent review → human gate → PR/artifacts → memory update`

## Hard defaults

- **Plan before mutating** (`AVI-AGENT-007`). Inspect the tree first.
- **Branch, never mutate main in place** (`AVI-AGENT-008`). PR is the handoff unit.
- **Skills ≠ project policy** (`AVI-AGENT-010`). Put reusable knowledge in `avi-*` skills; put repo rules in `AGENTS.md` / `PROJECT.yaml`.
- **Builder ≠ reviewer** (`AVI-AGENT-006`). After substantial code, run the `code-reviewer` agent (CodeRabbit). Do not treat self-check as the review.
- **Done means evidence** (`AVI-AGENT-028`): tests, typecheck/lint, diff, and for UI changes browser or equivalent verification.
- **Do not merge, deploy, pay, or delete production data** without an explicit human request (`AVI-AGENT-020`).
- **Secrets stay out of prompts and commits** (`AVI-AGENT-023`). Use env aliases; redact logs.
- Promote durable decisions out of chat into `PROJECT.yaml`, ADRs, `AGENTS.md`, or `kb/` (`AVI-AGENT-037`).

## This repo's overlays

Web app + AI/agent (`PROJECT.yaml` → `overlays`). Tenant isolation (`lib/tenant.ts`, `lib/mcp.ts`) is a security boundary: never hoist the MCP client; never accept `orgId` from the model.
